<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="05">
<name>Suspension</name>
<section id="1002I_S0016" variety="S0016">
<name>Suspension</name>
<ttl id="1002I_S0016_7450D_T00AO" variety="T00AO">
<name>Upper Control Arm Assembly Rear LH</name>
<para id="RM000001X3Y002X" category="A" type-id="80001" name-id="421GS-00" from="200612">
<name>Removal</name>
<subpara id="RM000001X3Y002X_02" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM000001X3Y002X_02_0005">
<ptxt>Remove Rear Tire</ptxt>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000001X3Y002X_02_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___000086300000">
<ptxt>Remove Upper Control Arm Assembly Rear LH</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a wooden block, jack up the rear axle carrier to the standard vehicle height as shown in the illustration, and support the rear suspension arm assembly No.2 LH.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C149535" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Remove the 2 bolts and 2 nuts, and remove the upper control arm assembly rear LH.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C149534" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Hold the nut and loosen the bolt.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>